Do not follow a whois referral that names no server.
A "whois:" line with nothing after the colon set the redirect to an
empty host name. IANA sends such a line for top-level domains without
a whois server, so whois printed "[Redirected to ]", tried to connect
to "", and failed with "bad address ''" (or connected to the local
machine, depending on the resolver) without showing the reply. Skip an
empty referral, so the reply is shown, or a later referral line is
used.

---
 networking/whois.c |    4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/networking/whois.c
+++ b/networking/whois.c
@@ -90,8 +90,8 @@
 				char *p = is_prefixed_with(linebuf, "whois server:");
 				if (!p)
 					p = is_prefixed_with(linebuf, "whois:");
-				if (p)
-					redir = xstrdup(skip_whitespace(p));
+				if (p && *(p = skip_whitespace(p)))
+					redir = xstrdup(p);
 			}
 		}
 	}
